  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "Fern-leaf maple. This popuand bold cultivar has large leaves with 9-13 cut lobes which divide almost to the leaf Each lobe is again deeply divided, the irregularly dissected, producing a fernappearance. The leaf form approaches that the monkshood genus, Aconitum. The inner of each lobe narrows almost to the giving an open form to the center of the The foliage is deep green, with tufts of at the vein junctions beneath. Fall colors brilliant scarlet shaded with carmine and purple. Clusters of maroon winged add to the attractiveness. This strong plant a round-topped small tree, reaching a of 16 ft. (5 m). It is one of the largestforms of the fullmoon maple and one of most desirable for any size landscape. Synonym, 'Maiku jaku' (meaning \"dancing peacock\")."
  },
